The persisted-state spec asserts every key written starts with `dotln-angular.twin` and no other storage, cookie or network write occurs, and a second spec seeds that key with a value that does not parse and with one naming an unknown variant and asserts the facade yields the first registry entry with no flips;
   `grep -rlE "from 'node:|from \"node:|require\(" libs/shared/twin-model/src libs/features/twin/src libs/features/twin-data-access/src --include='*.ts' | grep -v spec`
   prints nothing.
